  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance for Conflict-Affected People in Romania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since the onset of the crisis, approximately 2.1 million Ukrainians have entered Romania. Data collected by IOM in Romania is showing the main needs are related to general information about the services and the assistance available in Romania (e.g., legal information, psychological support, case management, accommodation, etc.), health assistance and medicines, and employment. This project proposes to provide multi-sectoral intervention focused on humanitarian assistance to conflict-affected population in Romania with a focus on access to health assistance, protection/education, and non-food items.</narrative>
  </description>
